Expert developer. Code and communication in English.

# Code Style (Clean Code)
- No comments unless necessary. Self-explanatory code.
- Naming: Clear, intention-revealing. Functions=verbs, variables=nouns. No abbreviations.
- Functions: Single responsibility, 20-40 lines. Max 3-4 params (use objects).
- Control Flow: Early returns, nesting ≤2. Avoid deep else-chains.
- Types: Explicit public APIs. Validate at boundaries (fail fast). Prefer immutability.
- Errors: Never swallow. Log actionable context.

# Git Workflow (Gitflow)
- Protected: `main`, `develop` (PRs required).
- Features: `feature/description` (from `develop` → `develop`).
- Bugfixes: `bugfix/description` (from `develop` → `develop`).
- Hotfixes: `hotfix/description` (from `main` → `main` AND `develop`).
- Releases: `release/vX.Y.Z` (from `develop` → `main` AND `develop`).
- CRITICAL: Verify branch. If on `develop`/`main`, create new branch first.

# Commit Messages (Gitmoji)
Format: `<gitmoji> <intent>: <message>`
✨ Feat, 🐛 Fix, ♻️ Refactor, 💄 UI/Style, 🎨 Structure, ⚡ Performance, 🔥 Remove, 📝 Docs, 🚀 Deploy, 🔒 Security, 🚧 WIP, 📦 Dependencies

# Architecture
- File size: 200-400 lines (split if >400).
- Single responsibility per file. No "God files".
- Exports: 1-3 related entities per file.
- Layers: Separate UI (components), domain (services/flows), data/infrastructure.
- Imports: Standard → Third-party → Internal (@/*).

# Testing (Vitest)
- Run `npm run test:ci` after changes, before commits, when fixing bugs.
- Test non-trivial logic. Arrange/Act/Assert pattern.
- Fast, deterministic, isolated tests.
- Before commit: `npm run test:ci` (lint + typecheck + tests).
- Before review: `npm run test:ci` + `coderabbit --prompt-only -t uncommitted`.
- Features: Write tests alongside (TDD when possible).
- Bugs: Add test reproducing bug, then fix.
- Refactoring: Run tests before/after.
- Coverage: Meaningful business logic + edge cases.
- Quick: `npm run test:run` for dev, `npm run test:ci` before commit.

# Tech Stack
- Framework: Next.js 15 (App Router)
- Language: TypeScript
- Styling: Tailwind CSS + Shadcn UI (Radix)
- Backend: Firebase (Auth, Firestore)
- State: React Context, Hooks

# CodeRabbit
- CLI available. Run: `coderabbit --prompt-only -t uncommitted`
- Use `--prompt-only` for token-efficient output.
- Use `-t uncommitted` for uncommitted changes only.
- Max 3 runs per change set.
- Help: `cr -h` or `coderabbit --help`
